*> How CALL names resolve: contained programs, COMMON programs of
*> containing programs, outermost programs and ENTRY points, and
*> what is left unresolved.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. OUTER.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  REC         PIC X(20).
01  TABLE-AREA.
    05  ROW     PIC X(4) OCCURS 5.
01  N           PIC 9(4) COMP.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    CALL "inner-a" USING REC
    CALL "INNER-B" USING ROW(2) BY CONTENT LENGTH OF REC
    CALL "ALT-ENTRY" USING BY VALUE N
    CALL "LIB" USING ROW REC(1:5) OMITTED
        ON EXCEPTION DISPLAY "no LIB"
    END-CALL
    CALL "SYSTEM" USING BY CONTENT "ls" RETURNING N
    STOP RUN.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. INNER-A IS COMMON.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01  L-REC       PIC X(20).
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-REC.
*>  INNER-B is not COMMON, so its sibling cannot call it.
    CALL "INNER-B" USING L-REC
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM INNER-A.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. INNER-B.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01  L-ROW       PIC X(4).
01  L-ANY       PIC X ANY LENGTH.
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ROW OPTIONAL L-ANY.
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM INNER-B.
END PROGRAM OUTER.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LIB.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01  L-N         PIC 9(4) COMP.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    GOBACK.
    ENTRY "ALT-ENTRY" USING BY VALUE L-N.
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM LIB.
